page RecipeKeepWritesMadeOffline(path: "/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline", title: "Keep writes made offline — Recipes", description: "Keep the reader's changes when the network drops: with sync on, a write that fails offline is kept and sent in order when the connection returns.") {
    RecipeShell("Keep writes made offline", summary: "Keep the reader's changes when the network drops, and send them when it comes back. This needs offline support turned on ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)), with `\"sync\": true` in its config:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Offer a new version", to: "/recipes/offer-a-new-version"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Make a site work offline", to: "/recipes/work-offline"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Translate a site", to: "/recipes/translate-a-site")], source: "md-docs/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline.md", how: true, hasVariations: false, project: { "src/pages/KeepWritesMadeOffline.wf": #"type Note { id: String, text: String }

api Backend(base: "/api") { }

api Backend.notes {
    get list() at "notes" -> [Note]!
    put save(id: String, body: Note) at "notes/{id}" -> Note!
        invalidates [list]
}

page Notes(path: "/notes", title: "Notes", description: "Notes that save offline.") {
    state draft = ""
    state said = ""
    Heading("Notes").h1
    Input(bind: draft, label: "Note")
    Button("Save") {
        on click {
            match await Backend.notes.save(id: "n1", body: Note(id: "n1", text: draft)) {
                .ok(_) { said = "Saved." }
                .err(.offline(true)) { said = "Saved here; it will be sent when you are back online." }
                .err(e) { said = e.message }
            }
        }
    }
    Text(said)
    if network.queued > 0 {
        Text("{network.queued} change(s) will be sent when you are back online").muted
    }
    for r in network.refused by r.at {
        Alert("The server refused a change ({r.status}).").danger
    }
    if network.refused.length > 0 {
        Button("Dismiss") { on click { network.clearRefused() } }
    }
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "keep-writes-made-offline",
  "offline": {
    "precache": [
      "/"
    ],
    "sync": true
  }
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** `offline` with `\"sync\": true` in `webfluent.app.json`, below, and a site served over HTTPS ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)).")
            CodeBlock(#"{ "offline": { "precache": ["/"], "sync": true } }"#, title: "json")
            Markdown("This page saves a note, says when the save is waiting for the connection, and lists any the server refused once they were sent:")
            CodeBlock(#"type Note { id: String, text: String }

api Backend(base: "/api") { }

api Backend.notes {
    get list() at "notes" -> [Note]!
    put save(id: String, body: Note) at "notes/{id}" -> Note!
        invalidates [list]
}

page Notes(path: "/notes", title: "Notes", description: "Notes that save offline.") {
    state draft = ""
    state said = ""
    Heading("Notes").h1
    Input(bind: draft, label: "Note")
    Button("Save") {
        on click {
            match await Backend.notes.save(id: "n1", body: Note(id: "n1", text: draft)) {
                .ok(_) { said = "Saved." }
                .err(.offline(true)) { said = "Saved here; it will be sent when you are back online." }
                .err(e) { said = e.message }
            }
        }
    }
    Text(said)
    if network.queued > 0 {
        Text("{network.queued} change(s) will be sent when you are back online").muted
    }
    for r in network.refused by r.at {
        Alert("The server refused a change ({r.status}).").danger
    }
    if network.refused.length > 0 {
        Button("Dismiss") { on click { network.clearRefused() } }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("With `sync` on, a write that is safe to send twice — a `PUT` or a `DELETE`, or a `POST` or `PATCH` its endpoint marks `idempotent` — that fails because the network is gone is kept. Its call still fails, as `.offline(queued: true)`: no answer came, so there is no value to show, and the page can say the change is waiting. A `POST` or `PATCH` that is not `idempotent` is not kept: one whose answer was lost may already have reached the server, so it fails as `.offline(queued: false)` and the page decides.\n\n`network.queued` is how many writes are waiting. Show it, as the page above does, so the reader knows their changes are safe.")

        Heading("What is kept", id: "what-is-kept").h3

        Markdown("Only a write that failed for want of a network is kept: the browser says it is offline, or the site's own server could not be reached. A request to another origin that is refused while the browser is online — a CORS refusal, a closed port — fails as it would without `sync`.\n\nA credential is never stored with a kept write. What an `api`'s `on request` hook adds — an `Authorization` header from the session — is added again when the write is sent, by the hook as it is then: a write made before a logout goes out with no one's token, never the old one. A write whose call carries a credential header itself (`headers: \{ \"Authorization\": token \}`) cannot be kept without it, so it is not kept, and its call fails as it would without `sync`.\n\nA `File` body is not kept, and its call fails as it would without `sync`.")

        Heading("When it is sent", id: "when-it-is-sent").h3

        Markdown("When the connection returns, the kept writes are sent in order:\n\n- by Background Sync, where the browser has it, so a closed tab still sends them;\n- by the page otherwise, the next time it is open.\n\nA server that takes the write makes stale what its endpoint `invalidates`: every read of those on an open page asks again, as it would after the write had gone at once. A server that refuses it — a `4xx` — has answered, so the write is not sent again; it is listed in `network.refused`, each `\{ method, url, status, at \}`, until `network.clearRefused()`. A server that is down, or asks the client to wait, keeps the write waiting for later.\n\nA write whose service adds credentials with its hook is sent by a page that has that service open, so the worker leaves it — and the writes after it, to keep them in order — for the next such page.")

        Heading("Forget the kept writes", id: "forget-the-kept-writes").h3

        Markdown("To forget every kept write — when the reader logs out, for example — call `WF.clearQueued()` from one of the project's scripts.")

    }
}
